{:edb/db-before-t 2315 :edb/db-after-t 2316 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535628 50 #inst "2026-10-14T19:34:14.874Z" 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186179714 1038 #edb/ref 17592186524114 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186179714 1038 #edb/ref 17592186524116 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186179714 1038 #edb/ref 17592186524124 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186179714 1040 #edb/ref 17592186524134 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524113 1080 "\\frac{4}{4 x + 5 y}\\,i+\\frac{5}{4 x + 5 y}\\,j" 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524113 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524113 1083 #uuid "187034c7-6c87-5c42-9dc7-1f516dfcbeb9" 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524114 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524126 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524114 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524114 1071 "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\ln{\\left(4 x + 5 y \\right)}.$" 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524114 1072 #uuid "1ea28d03-fccc-5031-9dd7-432a9072ff6e" 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524114 1074 "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $\\nabla f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(\\ln{\\left(4 x + 5 y \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{4}{4 x + 5 y} \\\\ f_{y}(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(\\ln{\\left(4 x + 5 y \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{5}{4 x + 5 y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla f(x,y)&=f_{x}(x,y)\\,i+f_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\ &= \\frac{4}{4 x + 5 y}\\,i+\\frac{5}{4 x + 5 y}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524115 1080 "\\frac{4}{4 x + y}\\,i+\\frac{1}{4 x + y}\\,j" 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524115 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524115 1083 #uuid "1f7b2c3c-dad5-5ea4-a872-ce1ccf3c8f77" 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524116 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524120 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524116 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524116 1071 "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\sin{\\left(x z + 4 y \\right)}.$" 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524116 1072 #uuid "3266754d-3a6d-5bf4-b53d-4b662bce4ae1" 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524116 1074 "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $\\nabla f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}(x,y,z)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(\\sin{\\left(x z + 4 y \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &=z \\cos{\\left(x z + 4 y \\right)} \\\\ f_{y}(x,y,z)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(\\sin{\\left(x z + 4 y \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &=4 \\cos{\\left(x z + 4 y \\right)} \\\\ f_{z}(x,y,z)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z}\\left(\\sin{\\left(x z + 4 y \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &=x \\cos{\\left(x z + 4 y \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla f(x,y,z)&=f_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+f_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+f_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\ &= z \\cos{\\left(x z + 4 y \\right)}\\,i+4 \\cos{\\left(x z + 4 y \\right)}\\,j+x \\cos{\\left(x z + 4 y \\right)}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524117 1080 "\\frac{1}{2 x + 6 y}\\,i+\\frac{1}{2 x + 6 y}\\,j" 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524117 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524117 1083 #uuid "39f4f022-3c40-5ef2-aed8-074e8335a6ed" 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524118 1080 "x \\cos{\\left(x z + 4 y \\right)}\\,i+4 y \\cos{\\left(x z + 4 y \\right)}\\,j+z \\cos{\\left(x z + 4 y \\right)}\\,k" 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17592186524118 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535628 17592186045443 true] [17